I think wishes would be OK, as long as they were sufficiently difficult to
puchase, money-wise.  Perhaps instead of a fixed price, they could charge
1000*level gp.

Instead of wishes, something slightly less powerful could be done:

Welcome to Possogronoe's Shop.  Do you wish to:
  :
  :
 (M) Mailorder    

This option would allow you to request an item in a way similar to a wish,
pay some bloated price for it (plus a hefty "shipping and handling fee") in
advance, and in a couple hundred turns or so (maybe longer), a mailer demon
can present you a scroll of mail or something similar notifying you that
your order has arrived and you can come pick it up.

